  "narration": {
    "description": "Eight stops and two short walking stories, from the Charterhouse to Exmouth Market: markets, print, flower-making and the watch trade. George throughout. About 2.75 km including the Farringdon approach; allow 75–90 minutes at a leisurely pace.",
    "introduction": "Begin at the Charterhouse exterior on the north side of Charterhouse Square, beyond Malmaison. From Farringdon, use the Cowcross Street exit; the map includes a roughly 7-minute public-street approach via Cowcross Street and Charterhouse Street. Read stop 1’s approach before setting off. Press Start only when you reach the Charterhouse: its story plays immediately. Eight exterior stops lead to Exmouth Market, with two short passages during the walk. Keep narration automatic for arrivals, or use I’m here / play story when needed. No building entry or purchase is required. This is an AI-created tour, researched against the sources saved with each story, with George’s synthetic narration.",
    "finishInstructions": "The tour ends on Exmouth Market. Tap End tour / stop location before settling down or heading home. For Farringdon, allow about 12–15 minutes: continue southwest to Vineyard Walk, follow it to Farringdon Road, then head south and turn towards the Cowcross Street station entrance, using pedestrian crossings. For Angel, allow about 15–18 minutes: return northeast along Exmouth to Rosoman Street, go north to Rosebery Avenue, follow it east to St John Street, then north towards the signed station entrance. These return walks are additional to the tour; there is no automatic rerouting.",
    "reviewNote": "Enjoy the walk first. A note at every stop is optional. The most useful feedback is what stayed with you, what place changed in your eyes, what dragged or confused you, and how the two walking passages fitted the walk. Review pauses narration; saving and closing it resumes an active tour. For dependable notes use Phone microphone and speak near the phone; Bluetooth microphone quality is still under investigation.",
    "rightsNote": "Original AI-assisted research, writing and local Kokoro George synthesis for Sidi’s private review. No paid or live generation during playback. Kokoro model/runtime provenance is retained with the preparation record; model Apache-2.0. Historical sources are linked per story; reconstruction is identified in its evidence. No third-party photographs or Street View images are bundled. Route/map data © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL, with Protomaps map attribution available on the map. Public distribution is a separate decision."
  },
